From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:04:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 29/34] media: mediatek: camraw: Both RAW engines by default

The captured requests split the frame between RAW-A and RAW-B, and RAW-A
alone overruns on the first line (phone run of 26.11, side A only). twin=0
stays for experiments.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/mediatek/camraw/mtk-camraw-drv.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/mediatek/camraw/mtk-camraw-drv.c b/drivers/media/platform/mediatek/camraw/mtk-camraw-drv.c
index ad4b89723fd2..353e2b6acb61 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/mediatek/camraw/mtk-camraw-drv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/mediatek/camraw/mtk-camraw-drv.c
@@ -89,9 +89,9 @@ static char *frame_fw = "titan2/camraw-frame.bin";
 module_param(frame_fw, charp, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(frame_fw, "Steady request applied for every frame, below the firmware directory");
 
-static bool twin;
+static bool twin = true;
 module_param(twin, bool, 0644);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(twin, "Run both RAW engines as captured (1), or only the side A descriptors (0, left part of the picture)");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(twin, "Run both RAW engines as captured (1, default), or only the side A descriptors (0: RAW-A alone overruns on the first line; for experiments)");
 
 static unsigned int reapply = 1;
 module_param(reapply, uint, 0644);
-- 
